explanation.unicode:
The standard equation of a travelling wave is y = A cos(omega t - k x).
Comparing it with the given equation y = 5 cos left(200π t - (π x/150)right), we find:
Angular frequency omega = 200πtext{ rad/s}
Wave number k = (π/150)text{ cm}^{-1}
The velocity of the wave is given by v = (omega/k):
v = (200π/π / 150) = 200 × 150 = 30000text{ cm/s}
Converting to meters per second:
v = 300text{ m/s}.
